// What an import inside the module tree refuses: a path that walks to a
// neighbour, and a module naming the module that contains it.
//
// The whole scenario is the folder, because every diagnostic is reported against
// a file this one never names: what is under test is which module a written path
// may reach, and the layout is the case.
//
// Parse stage, which is why it is its own scenario: a parse diagnostic stops the
// compile before name resolution.
//
// The folder holds:
//   alpha/alpha.cone         spells a path to its sister beta
//   beta/beta.cone           the sister both paths arrive at
//   outer/outer.cone         a submodule with a submodule of its own
//   outer/inner/inner.cone   names its parent, and spells a path to its
//                            parent's sister

mod module_import_reject;

fn designated() i64 {
  1i64;
}
